+### Specialty directory
+
+<a id="req-vet-003"></a>
+
+The clinic also publishes the inverse view of that directory: every specialty it knows, each with the veterinarians holding it. Staff open it to answer "which veterinarians hold this specialty" `[REQ-VET-003]`. Each veterinarian is shown by full name — first name, then last name. A veterinarian holding no specialty appears nowhere, because the page lists specialties rather than the whole roster `[REQ-VET-003]`. The page offers no search or filter, and every specialty appears on one page. It is reached by its own address, `/specialties.html`, which nothing links to `[REQ-VET-003]`.
+
+**Done when:**
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given the clinic's specialties, when the specialty directory is opened at `/specialties.html`, then every specialty is listed by its stored name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty that veterinarians hold, when the directory is opened, then each of them is shown under it by first name then last name.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a veterinarian holding no specialty, when the directory is opened, then that veterinarian appears nowhere on the page.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given a specialty held by no veterinarian, when the directory is opened, then it is still listed, with no veterinarian under it.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given more specialties than one screen holds, when the directory is opened, then all of them appear on one page and no paging control is offered.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given unchanged stored data, when the directory is opened twice, then specialties appear in name order and each specialty's veterinarians in the same order both times.
+- `[REQ-VET-003]` given any page of the system, when it is rendered, then no link or navigation entry points at the specialty directory.
+
+**Edge cases:**
+1. A veterinarian holding more than one specialty is listed under each of them.
+2. A clinic that knows no specialty renders an empty directory rather than a failure.
+3. Specialty names are stored data. They are shown as stored and are not part of the translated wording that `REQ-LANG-002` governs.
+
+**Design:** [system-design.md#contracts](system-design.md#contracts)
+
